+/* Hands at rest, as macOS tells them apart: by where a touch lands, not by
+ * whether any key is held. A touch that begins in the bottom strip is a thumb
+ * resting there; one that begins in the outer strips either side shortly after
+ * typing is the heel of a hand. Both are ignored (pointer, taps, clickfinger,
+ * gestures) until they travel far enough to be a finger reaching in. */
